## Common Tasks

{% if stack in ["python-fastapi", "python-fastapi-nextjs", "fullstack-desktop"] %}
### Add an API route

1. Create `backend/src/api/routes/<resource>.py`
2. Define a `router = APIRouter(prefix="/v1/<resource>", tags=["<resource>"])`
3. Register in `backend/src/api/main.py`: `app.include_router(resource_router)`
4. Add auth dependency: `Depends(require_auth)` on protected endpoints
5. Write at least one integration test in `backend/tests/integration/test_<resource>.py`

### Add a DB model

1. Define the SQLAlchemy model in `backend/src/database/models/<entity>.py`
2. Import it in `backend/src/database/models/__init__.py` so Alembic sees it
3. Generate migration: `uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add <entity>"`
4. Review the generated migration file — always check for destructive ops
5. Apply: `uv run alembic upgrade head`
6. Add a repository class in `backend/src/database/repos/<entity>_repo.py`

### Add a background task

1. Add the job function to `backend/src/worker/tasks.py`
2. Enqueue via Redis Streams producer in the route handler
3. Register the consumer in `backend/src/worker/consumer.py`
{% endif %}

{% if stack in ["nextjs-fullstack", "python-fastapi-nextjs", "fullstack-desktop"] %}
### Add a frontend page

1. Create `frontend/src/app/(dashboard)/<route>/page.tsx`
2. If the page needs data, add the API call to `frontend/src/lib/api.ts`
3. Wrap in a TanStack Query hook: `frontend/src/hooks/use<Resource>.ts`
4. Add the nav link to the sidebar/nav component

### Add a UI component

1. Check if a shadcn/ui primitive covers the need first (`npx shadcn-ui add <component>`)
2. If custom, create in `frontend/src/components/<domain>/<ComponentName>.tsx`
3. Use Tailwind for styling — no inline styles, no CSS modules
4. Export from the domain barrel: `frontend/src/components/<domain>/index.ts`

### Add a Zustand store

1. Create `frontend/src/stores/<domain>Store.ts`
2. Define the state interface and actions
3. Export a typed hook: `export const use<Domain>Store = create<State>()(...)`
{% endif %}

{% if stack == "python-cli" %}
### Add a CLI command

1. Add a new `@cli.command()` in `src/cli.py` (or a sub-group file)
2. Use `typer` types for arguments and options — never `sys.argv`
3. Add a test in `tests/test_cli.py` using `typer.testing.CliRunner`
{% endif %}

